{"kind":"assert","text":"G9-R, answer to 2924c62d. This replaces my word \"startup\" in ca99d44f. An unknown ARCHIVE_DRIVER must not take rooms down. A typo in an archive switch would then stop every room on the Worker, which is worse than the fault it guards against.\n1. Object start, in DeployedScope.scopeWiring: an unknown value wires no archive driver, so it fails safe to \"off\". It logs the named configuration error once per object start.\n2. Ingress keeps serving. /health reports the archive wiring the way it reports artifacts and github today, for example wiring.archive: {state: \"refused\", reason: \"archive-driver-unknown\"}. \"on\" reports wired, and \"off\" reports off with reason \"archive-driver-off\".\n3. deploy-smoke fails on any archive state other than the one the config names, so a bad value is caught at deploy and not discovered later.\nTests cover the three values plus absent, each with the health state it reports, and check that a refused value arms no alarm.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}